# Citation File Format (CFF) for PMxAgent
# This file provides metadata for citing PMxAgent in academic publications
# See: https://citation-file-format.github.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PMxAgent: An Agentic Platform for Pharmacometrics"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-01-07
abstract: |
  PMxAgent is an open-source framework that transforms validated R pharmacometric
  workflows into AI-ready HTTP APIs using Docker containerization and the Model
  Context Protocol (MCP). It provides three core pharmacometric endpoints:
  non-compartmental analysis (NCA), exposure-response (ER) modeling, and
  pharmacokinetic (PK) simulation. PMxAgent enables AI agents like Cursor and
  Claude Code to discover and use pharmacometric tools automatically, bridging
  the gap between trusted R analytics and modern AI-driven automation systems.

authors:
  - family-names: Bloomingdale
    given-names: Peter
    email: pbloomingdale@generatebiomedicines.com
    affiliation: "Translational PKPD and Clinical Pharmacology, Generate Biomedicines"
  - family-names: Khot
    given-names: Antari

repository-code: "https://github.com/peterbloomingdale/PMxAgent"
url: "https://github.com/peterbloomingdale/PMxAgent"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/peterbloomingdale/PMxAgent/blob/main/LICENSE"

keywords:
  - pharmacometrics
  - pharmacokinetics
  - non-compartmental analysis
  - exposure-response
  - model context protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agents
  - R
  - Plumber
  - Docker
  - FastMCP
  - automation
  - API

